  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-cost-test/a-probed-entity-is-sought-not-scanned}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-nested-call-in-a-predicate-is-refused"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by step E run #11 (2026-10-23, design run seon.context/e11-map-from-program#1, turn 3): `(d/q '[:find ?n :where [?e :ns/name ?n] [(clojure.string/ends-with? (str ?n) \"-test\")]] db)` answers no rows on a db holding 47 such namespaces, where binding first, `[(str ?n) ?s] [(clojure.string/ends-with? ?s \"-test\")]`, answers 47. Datalog takes no nested expression in a predicate (Datomic refuses the query), so the empty answer is a swallowed error: the model read it as no test namespaces and went exploring. Correct, in Datahike's query parser (a jolt/<topic> fork branch): a predicate or function clause whose argument is a list is refused with the clause named. Proof: that query raises, naming the clause.
Cause found 2026-10-23 (branch jolt/nested-call-refused): the parser reads (str ?n) as a constant list, -call-fn passes it to the predicate, and filter-by-pred reads the ClassCastException as false. Refused at the parse by datahike.query/refuse-nested-calls (Datahike dda24c0), a quoted form too unless it is q's query. The catch that read the error as false remains: task datahike.query/a-predicate-that-throws-is-an-error."
